*To start your thesis, follow @subsec:getting_started.* The rest of this document shows each feature of the template; the Typst code that produces it is in the matching file in `chapters/`.

This Typst template typesets doctoral theses, or any long document of a similar format, in two editions: one to print and one to read on screen. It is not affiliated with any university, so before you submit, confirm with your supervisor and doctoral school that it meets their requirements. It derives from the Modern UiT Thesis Template by Moritz Jörg and Ole Tytlandsvik #footnote[see #link("https://github.com/mrtz-j/typst-thesis-template")], a Typst port of Erlend Graff's #LaTeX template for UiT The Arctic University of Norway #footnote[see #link("https://github.com/egraff/uit-thesis")].

The chapters cover:
+ @chp:basic_usage: the file structure and how to start a thesis;
+ @chp:figures: images, tables, listings, subfigures, equations and theorems;
+ @chp:typst_basics: headings, lists, text styling, footnotes and citations;
+ @chp:utilities: comments while writing, signature forms, publications and abbreviations.
